---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import FaqAccordion from '@/components/FaqAccordion.astro';
import TeamFinder from '@/components/TeamFinder.astro';
import { teams } from '@/data/teams';
import { parentFaqs } from '@/data/parent-faqs';
---
<BaseLayout title="Parent Resources | AZGYL" pathname="/parents">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Parents" title="Everything a parent should need before the first game." intro="Use this page as the decision engine: find the right age group, find the nearest team, buy the right gear, understand placement, and get answers without hunting through multiple websites." image="/assets/heroes/parents-hero.svg" />

  <section>
    <div class="container stack-lg">
      <div class="section-header-clean section-header-clean--action">
        <div>
          <div class="section-kicker">Start here</div>
          <h2>Parent hub</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-header-copy">
          <p>Start with the team directory, confirm the age group, get the right gear, and use these pages for the questions families ask every season.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <nav class="subpage-links" aria-label="Parent quick links">
        <a href="/teams">Find your club</a>
        <a href="#equipment">Equipment</a>
        <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
        <a href="/parents/role">Parent expectations</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <article class="metric"><div class="section-kicker">Step 1</div><h3>Find the closest current team.</h3><p>Use city, district, or zip code to find the best current fit. Once boundaries are finalized, this can switch to official placement logic.</p></article>
        <article class="metric"><div class="section-kicker">Step 2</div><h3>Register and complete membership.</h3><p>Sign up through the local program, complete USA Lacrosse membership, and confirm where communication for your team will live.</p></article>
        <article class="metric"><div class="section-kicker">Step 3</div><h3>Gear up and show up ready.</h3><p>Buy the required basics, arrive early, and let the coaches handle the learning curve from there.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container finder-grid finder-grid-parents">
      <div class="finder-inline stack-lg">
        <div class="copy stack-md">
          <div class="section-kicker">Age groups</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading section-heading--plain">Find your player’s division in seconds.</h2>
          <p class="section-sidecopy">Use the grade selector for the fastest answer. This is a rec guide rail, not a compliance trap.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="choice-row" data-grade-buttons>
          <button type="button" data-grade="2">K–2</button>
          <button type="button" data-grade="4">3–4</button>
          <button type="button" data-grade="6">5–6</button>
          <button type="button" data-grade="8">7–8</button>
        </div>
        <div class="result-shell" data-age-result>
          <div class="note">Recommended division</div>
          <strong>Choose a grade band</strong>
          <p>We will show the best starting division and link you to the full age chart PDF.</p>
          <div class="actions"><a class="button button-outline button-sm" href="/resources/age-chart">Open age chart</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <TeamFinder teams={teams} variant="compact" title="Find your club" intro="Search by city, district, or zip. Results are broad-match suggestions until official boundaries are finalized." actionLabel="Open full directory" directoryHref="/teams" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="equipment">
    <div class="container section-block stack-lg">
      <div class="section-header-clean">
        <div>
          <div class="section-kicker">Equipment</div>
          <h2>Buy the required basics first.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-header-copy"><p>For most girls field players, the must-have list is short: stick, mouthguard, protective eyewear, and practical cleats or field shoes. Keep the first purchase simple and skip the panic spending spiral.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <article class="metric"><h3>Stick</h3><p>Start with a legal girls stick that feels manageable in the player’s hands. Fancy is not the point in season one.</p></article>
        <article class="metric"><h3>Protective eyewear</h3><p>Required for girls field players and worth fitting correctly the first time so it stays comfortable.</p></article>
        <article class="metric"><h3>Mouthguard</h3><p>Mandatory. Buy two so one lives in the bag and one stays at home.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt" id="first-practice">
    <div class="container two-col split-balanced">
      <div class="copy stack-md">
        <div class="section-kicker">First practice checklist</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">What to have ready before you leave the house.</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Stick, mouthguard, eyewear, and cleats packed the night before</li>
          <li>Water bottle filled and labeled</li>
          <li>Practice location confirmed with arrival 10–15 minutes early</li>
          <li>Coach or team-manager contact saved in your phone</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="copy stack-md">
        <div class="section-kicker">What to expect</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">What the first week usually feels like for new families.</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>1–4 practices per week depending on age group and field access</li>
          <li>Basic stick work, movement, spacing, and team expectations</li>
          <li>A lot of new vocabulary and zero need to already know it all</li>
          <li>A season structure that gets clearer once schedules are finalized</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq">
    <div class="container stack-lg">
      <div class="section-header-clean">
        <div>
          <div class="section-kicker">Questions parents ask every season</div>
          <h2>Get the common answers in one place.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-header-copy"><p>Use the FAQ for start-up questions. Use the rules and code-of-conduct pages when the answer affects placement, eligibility, or behavior.</p></div>
      </div>
      <FaqAccordion items={parentFaqs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    const result = document.querySelector('[data-age-result]');
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-grade-buttons] button').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const grade = Number(button.dataset.grade || 0);
        let division = '8U';
        if (grade <= 2) division = '8U';
        else if (grade <= 4) division = '10U';
        else if (grade <= 6) division = '12U';
        else division = '14U';
        result.innerHTML = `<div class="note">Recommended division</div><strong>${division}</strong><p>This is the best starting point for most players in this grade band. Final placement can still depend on school affiliation and roster needs.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-outline button-sm" href="/resources/age-chart">Open age chart</a></div>`;
      });
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
